decision 5" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=2;rounded=0;fillColor=#d4e1f5;strokeColor=#3d6fa8;fontSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2500" y="1350" width="560" height="115" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ae123" value="variant selected by
root cause + audience" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#4d4d4d;strokeColor=#3d6fa8;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.2;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="An113" target="An115"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="An124" value="EVERY DRAFT CARRIES TWO TIERS

outbound_draft
supplier-visible content only;
this is what lands in the mailbox

review_panel
helpdesk-only data + full evidence
chain; lives in the reviewer
application, NEVER in the mailbox

Why: a draft stored in the group
mailbox (FR3) can be sent by anyone
with access, bypassing review.
Past failed payments, bank context
and PA allocation data are
helpdesk-only per both scenario tabs." style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3090" y="440" width="340" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="An125" value="OPEN DECISIONS AFFECTING OUTPUT

N-13 / N-03  reply policy when one
email names n invoices and only some
resolve: one consolidated reply or
one per invoice?

N-26  which finding leads when
several coexist (US-04 forbids
forcing a single cause)

N-21  draft authority: mailbox copy
or case-store copy?

N-22  reviewer edit governance -
edited text has not passed FR13
grounding

N-29  internal outcomes (D5) are
never observed: no write-back exists" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;dashed=1;fontColor=#b85450;fontStyle=2;fontSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3090" y="870" width="340" height="420" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="An126" value="REQUESTER RETURN PATH

D3 and D2 return to the supplier in
the SAME thread. A supplier reply is
correlated by conversation_id (FR5,
P17) and APPENDS to the open case
rather than opening a new one.

This is what makes the missing-
information path a pause, not a
termination." style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3090" y="1320" width="340" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ae127" value="reply to requester in thread; correlated back by conversation_id (FR5)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=8;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#4d4d4d;dashed=1;strokeColor=#82b366;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="An117" target="An12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="An129" value="Input / interface object" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2295" width="140" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="An130" value="Deterministic component" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="190" y="2295" width="140" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
